  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policies, strategies and/or innovative interventions to promote productive employment and decent work are implemented in Belize</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This area of focus supports the Government of Belize and social partners in implementing the Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP), focusing on productive employment, efficient labour market programmes, and enhanced data systems. Efforts include developing a National Employment Policy (NEP) through employment diagnostics, social dialogue, and creating an action plan, monitoring framework, and resource estimation. It also strengthens stakeholders&apos; capacity for NEP development and implementation. To enhance labour market programmes, interventions support the creation of a five-year Public Employment Services (PES) action plan, prioritizing integration, key job services, and capacity-building for employment officers. Additionally, it advances social justice by improving labour market statistics, providing technical assistance for employment modules in censuses, and aligning national labour force surveys with global standards. These initiatives aim for comprehensive, data-driven, and inclusive employment solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
